-\subsection{Architecture-family falsification}
-Figure~\ref{fig:arch} separates the robust local endpoint from its cohort-dependent ranking consequence. On fastMRI, disjoint-minus-shared observable-error gain is 17.8/17.6/8.0/13.7/22.6 points for HAT/SwinIR/I3Net/SAINT/CycleINR; all clustered intervals exclude zero. The independently frozen IXI replication gives 29.0/30.2/25.2/29.8/29.6 points, with all five intervals above zero and all 115 case effects positive for every model. Reflection-balanced identity-swap estimates remain 29.2/30.0/25.1/29.7/29.5 points, and all five mirror-difference intervals include zero. The IXI equal-weight four-family estimate is 28.6 points; leave-one-family-out estimates remain 28.1--29.7 points. Phase-0 wrapper maximum error is zero for all ten cohort--model runs.
+\subsection{Replication: local geometry is stronger than ranking}
+Across five architectures, fastMRI local observable gains range from 8.0 to 22.6 percentage points and IXI gains from 25.2 to 30.2. All five-model simultaneous intervals remain positive, including all four within-/between-case mean/median sensitivity combinations. Every IXI case effect is positive for each model. Reflection-balanced identity-swap estimates remain positive, while all five mirror-difference intervals include zero; this constrains a particular geometry alternative, not all confounding.
 
