+The central limitations are concrete. Analyses repeatedly inspect the same cohorts, some controls and endpoints evolved after results, and filesystem dates do not establish prespecification. Historical influence masks and normalization use targets. Interventions leave residual geometry, boundary and preprocessing differences. NingXia has eight independent patients; the five-architecture study covers brain T2, not a matched neural knee replication. Adapted implementations and imperfect historical training/validation separation limit architecture interpretation. Statistical intervals quantify sampling uncertainty conditional on the chosen analyses, not selection uncertainty from the full research history.
 
-Figure~\ref{fig:consequence} evaluates acquired-anchor cross-validation as a consequence, not the central novelty. Anchor-CV ranks $\times4$ examination error with $\rho=.943/.955/.958$ on fastMRI/IXI/NingXia. Adjacent MAE gives .934/.956/.973 and adjacent RMSE .942/.956/.959; paired differences are not consistently significant. Conditional association beyond adjacent MAE, scale, and spacing is .333/$-.059$/$-.100$. Anchor-CV is therefore an interpretable acquired-only difficulty signal, not unique information.
-
-Matching model labels removes a cross-architecture switch, but factor-specific checkpoints can differ. Across 13 models, Anchor-CV has positive within-model association with $\times4\!\rightarrow\!\times2$ benefit for 13/13 fastMRI and 12/13 NingXia models, with median $\rho=.851/.727$. Adjacent MAE gives 13/13 and 12/13 (median .802/.748); candidate-bank disagreement gives 11/11 and 10/11 (median .835/.710). All three non-positive NingXia directions belong to the severely degraded Res-SRDiff run and all corresponding intervals cross zero; the run is retained rather than redefining eligibility. Controlling current $\times4$ MAE reduces Anchor-CV median partial $\rho$ to .203/.291; all 26 clustered intervals cross zero. A recovered 115-case IXI I3Net same-architecture analysis gives $\rho=.843$ [.768,.894], versus .845 [.771,.896] for adjacent MAE. Acquired-range normalization reverses these raw-benefit rankings to $-.238/-.236$. Normalizing both score and benefit instead yields $.539/.551$ on IXI. Thus benefit ranking depends on its unit convention and current difficulty, not only acquisition value.
