-We apply fixed linear (L) and four-point Lagrange cubic (C) estimators to 125 TopCoW MRA cases with vascular annotations~\cite{yang2026topcow}, covering 10779 common missing planes. L$_0$--C$_0$ versus L$_0$--C$_2$, and C$_0$--L$_0$ versus C$_0$--L$_2$, keep the estimator pairing fixed while changing anchor identity. Both residues are averaged equally within cases. The score mask uses only phase-0 acquired anchors; labels define evaluation endpoints only. Observable gains are 34.5 [34.4,34.6] and 34.5 [34.4,34.6] points under two-pair simultaneous intervals. This is an analytical external check, not a neural MRA replication. Fixed phase-0 error and annotated-vessel ranking are separately reported in the supplement.
